Actually, in aevol: "Pirates: an event in the world that occurs when the score exceeds a certain threshold (score > 5?) and steals points from each agent" — I recall that in the monarch/military-democratic regime pirates appear, and the pirate raid threshold was a score of…. Details: in the paper, pirate raids occur when the world score exceeds a threshold, and each pirate steals points from an agent. There are also "immortal agents" (rulers) and "plankton". Death: all agents have a finite lifespan, but "immortals" can avoid death by moving between bodies (leaders). Hmm — I shouldn't over-specify. Flag it as an uncertainty with a researcher topic.

