archy is a world property that emerges; no randomization over it. Interaction claims downgrade to *associational*, identified only conditional on measured hierarchy plus world-level covariates; treat as pre-registered quasi-experimental secondary estimand.\n- **Event arms:** **B0** off; **B1** built-in threshold; **B2** shifted/unreachable threshold; **B2\u2032** exogenous schedule matched to B1's empirical invasion-time distribution (requires C8; if C8 needs code injection, see F6).\n\n## 2. Estimand (stated before any estimator)\n\n**In words.** For agents eligible at run start, the causal contrast in survival duration between worlds where the event mechanic operates (triggered by score threshold or schedule) and worlds where it is disabled \u2014 and specifically whether that contrast *differs* between hierarchical and non-hierarchical worlds.\n\n**Notation.** For event arm *a* \u2208 {B0, B1, B2\u2032} and hierarchy *h* \u2208 {H, F}: S<sub>a,h</sub>(t) = P(T > t | do(arm a, regime h)), T = time from t=0 to all-cause death, administratively censored at \u03c4 (fixed horizon).\n\n**Primary estimand (RMST scale):**\n\u0394 = [RMST<sub>B1,H</sub>(\u03c4) \u2212 RMST<sub>B0,H</sub>(\u03c4)] \u2212 [RMST<sub>B1,F</sub>(\u03c4) \u2212 RMST<sub>B0,F</sub>(\u03c4)], RMST<sub>a,h</sub>(\u03c4) = \u222b\u2080^\u03c4 S<sub>a,h</sub>(t)dt.\n**Secondary (hazard scale):** interaction coefficient \u03b2\u2083 in \u03bb(t | a, h, X) = \u03bb\u2080(t)\u00b7exp(\u03b2\u2081a + \u03b2\u2082h + **\u03b2\u2083\u00b7a\u00b7h** + \u03b3\u2032X), reported with the standard caveat that hazard-ratio interaction is non-collapsible and dependent on baseline-hazard shape \u2014 hence RMST \u0394 is primary.\n\n**The score-gating problem, explicitly.** Event *occurrence time* = first passage of world score through the threshold. Score accumulation is post-baseline and plausibly hierarchy-influenced, so exposure is a **post-treatment, hierarchy-influenced variable**. The naive B1-only comparison (hierarchical vs. flat worlds, both with events) confounds the event effect with (i) baseline hierarchy\u2192survival differences and (ii) differential exposure timing (hierarchies may reach threshold sooner). Identification roles:\n\n- **B0 (arm contrast B1 vs B0 within each h):** identifies the total event effect within regime; under V-A both arms' world assignment is exogenous, so no post-baseline conditioning is needed. This is the workhorse; it does *not* identify within-B1 cross-regime contrasts.\n- **B2\u2032 (exogenous schedule):** severs score\u2192event, making exposure a baseline-assigned intervention. **Buys:** a timing/susceptibility interaction free of survivor-censoring of exposure. **Costs:** it answers a *different question* (\"invasions at tick t\") than the built-in mechanic (\"invasions when score hits X\", whose timing agents may causally influence). Report both; do not pool.\n- **Conditioning on the score process:** I classify endogenous score as a **mediator** of hierarchy\u2192exposure\u2192survival, *not* a confounder of the arm contrast (arm assignment precedes score). Primary analysis therefore conditions on baseline score only. A score-conditioned hazard model is *secondary*, interpreted as a controlled-direct-effect-like contrast, with the explicit warning that time-varying conditioning on a mediator blocks part of the causal path (overadjustment) and opens collider paths on unmeasured world factors; a sequential g-formula version is the pre-registered sensitivity analysis.\n\n## 3. Design hygiene (part of the deliverable)\n\n**Units and dependence.** Unit of **randomization: the world** (one seeded run; hierarchy under V-A is a world/regime property). Unit of **observation: the agent**, nested in worlds; worlds sharing a seed across arms are **paired** (shared-stream block). Agents within a world share environment, score pool, RNG stream, and events \u21d2 correlated survival. Estimation clusters on world (world-level bootstrap / robust SEs / shared frailty); seed-pairing is exploited by paired contrasts, never by pretending agents independent.\n\n**Sample size without an ICC (no fabricated effect sizes).** Cells = 2 (hierarchy) \u00d7 arms (B0, B1, \u00b1B2\u2032) with seed-pairing. Justification is decision-theoretic, in three pre-registered steps: (1) **budget bound** \u2014 N per cell capped by wall-clock-per-world \u00d7 cells from feasibility check F4; (2) **precision target** \u2014 pre-specify a minimum decision-relevant interaction \u03b4_min *qualitatively* with the domain owner, then size N \u2265 4\u00b7Var(RMST per world)/\u03b4_min\u00b2\u00b7z\u00b2, where Var is **estimated in a pre-registered 5-world pilot on the two corner cells (B0/B1 \u00d7 H/F)** \u2014 a pilot measurement, not an assumed number; (3) **interim precision check** after first 30 worlds/cell, expandable to the cap; stopping rule based on CI width only, never on significance. The \"30\u2013100\" range is exactly this pilot-and-expand band; under V-B, power for the interaction comes mainly from within-world agent contrasts and is weaker \u2014 stated, not hidden.\n\n**Censoring and competing risks.** Run-end censoring is administrative and arm-independent by construction \u21d2 KM/Cox valid. Invasions might kill directly *and* via point loss that later causes death. The primary outcome is **all-cause** time-to-death, for which competing risks are irrelevant (all causes share one terminal event). Cause-specific structure matters only for the mechanistic secondary analysis: report Aalen\u2013Johansen CIFs and cause-specific hazards descriptively; a single all-cause hazard is adequate for the primary estimand precisely because \"how the event kills\" is on the causal path, not a competing treatment assignment. If a resurrection/immortality mechanic exists (unverifiable \u2014 see \u00a76), agents with it are either excluded by eligibility or stratified; pre-declared once the code check resolves it.\n\n**Survivor selection into exposure (the key attack).** If one analyzes \"agents exposed to an invasion vs. not,\" exposure conditions on (a) having survived to the invasion and (b) one's world reaching the threshold \u2014 both affected by hierarchy and frailty. Hierarchical worlds reaching threshold *later* or with fewer surviving agents produce an exposed stratum selected for survivorship; immortal-time bias is guaranteed (an agent must survive to invasion #1 to contribute post-invasion person-time). **Remedy \u2014 the primary analysis never compares exposed vs. unexposed agents.** It is a **target trial / ITT emulation**: eligibility fixed at t=0 (agents present at run start); treatment = the world's assigned arm, fixed at assignment before any score or death exists; follow-up t=0\u2192\u03c4; analysis by assigned arm. ITT is immune to post-baseline selection because arm precedes exposure. Within-arm \"effect of an actual invasion\" (time-varying post-invasion hazard) is *secondary*, fitted only as a counting-process Cox with **delayed entry at the world's invasion time** (left truncation), labeled subject-within-world frailty and interpretation-limited.\n**Falsification of the interaction claim.** The interaction is rejected (attributed to survivor selection or timing rather than differential event susceptibility) if any of: (i) \u0394's world-bootstrap CI is not separated from a null band computed by seed-pair permutations; (ii) the **B2\u2032 exogenous arm shows no interaction** while B1 does (\u21d2 the B1 \"interaction\" is exposure-timing \u00d7 selection, not susceptibility); (iii) the **negative-control contrast B0 vs B0\u2032** (identical configs differing only in inert logging/no-op parameters) shows a spurious interaction; (iv) a **landmark re-estimation** at \u03c4\u2080 chosen before the earliest invasion in any arm \u2014 restricting eligibility to agents alive at \u03c4\u2080 with risk sets properly restarted \u2014 attenuates \u0394 to null.\n\n## 4. Full protocol\n\n- **Cells (V-A core):** {H, F} \u00d7 {B0, B1, B2\u2032}; optional B2 (shifted threshold) as a dose-finding/threshold-robustness arm.\n- **Controls:** identical seed set reused across all cells (paired streams); matched initial populations per seed; single-parameter changes between arms; fixed \u03c4 and identical logging overhead in every arm (B0\u2032 sham arm carries the same logging as B1); pre-registered single primary contrast family (\u0394), all else secondary/exploratory.\n- **Analysis:** (1) KM per cell; RMST(\u03c4) via world-level bootstrap (resample worlds; keep seed pairs intact) \u2192 \u0394 and CI. (2) Cox shared-gamma-frailty, cluster = world, covariates arm, hierarchy, arm\u00d7hierarchy + baseline-only covariates; Efron ties; PH diagnostics; Weibull-AFT sensitivity. (3) Paired-seed difference-in-differences of world RMST with sign-flip permutation test. (4) Secondary: delayed-entry within-arm invasion-response Cox; Aalen\u2013Johansen cause CIFs; sequential g-formula with time-varying score (controlled-direct-effect-like, collider-caveated); leader-vs-follower strata (V-A only). (5) Under V-B: same pipeline with measured hierarchy in place of the randomized factor, labeled associational.\n- **Deliverable artifacts:** registered protocol + analysis code before any compute; target-trial specification table (eligibility/assignment/follow-up/estimand/analysis).\n\n## 5. Pre-registered feasibility checks on the real code (run before spending compute)\n\n| Check | Test | If it fails \u2192 what degrades |\n|---|---|---|\n| F1 Event toggle exists (C1) | config diff; B0 trace has zero invasions | Arms collapse to on/off only; B2 dropped; threshold-dose claims withdrawn |\n| F2 Seed determinism (C6) | same seed twice \u21d2 byte-identical trace | Pairing, paired permutation tests, and variance reduction void; raise N; randomization audit needed |\n| F3 Per-tick score logging cheap (C5) | profile overhead | Score becomes piecewise/checkpointed; time-varying mediator analyses coarsen; g-formula sensitivity weakened |\n| F4 Wall-clock per world \u00d7 cells vs budget | 1-world timing run | B2/B2\u2032 arms and the upper end of N dropped; 2\u00d72 core preserved |\n| F5 Hierarchy assignable (C3) | regime toggle exists? | V-A \u2192 V-B; interaction downgraded to associational; hierarchy matched strata added |\n| F6 Exogenous scheduling (C8) | injection point in event scheduler without altering other behavior | B2\u2032 dropped \u21d2 timing-vs-susceptibility disambiguation lost; the design's main defense (\u00a73) is left open \u2014 declared as residual weakness |\n| F7 Lifecycle log with cause codes (C4) | inspect event stream | Outcome misclassification risk; validate inferred deaths by manual trace review of a few runs |\n| F8 Threshold param (C2) | value change alters first-invasion tick | B2 arm dropped |\n\n## 6. \"Unverifiable here\" register\n\nCodebase identity (the aevol hypothesis), the actual threshold value and comparison direction, death/termination rules, existence of immortals/respawn, whether invasions kill directly or only via point theft, whether hierarchy is a regime setting or emergent, score semantics \u2014 **none observed**; no code exists in this environment and nothing here was executed. Every simulator-specific element above is contract-gated and routes to a row in \u00a75.\n\n---\n\n**Rationale summary.** The question is a moderation question (\"does the event mechanic affect survival differently by hierarchy\"), and score-gating makes exposure post-baseline. The design therefore (i) randomizes at the world level at t=0 and analyzes ITT-style, (ii) uses RMST interaction as the primary, collapsible estimand with a hazard-scale secondary, (iii) adds an exogenous-schedule arm and landmark/permutation/negative-control falsification checks specifically to kill the survivor-selection alternative, and (iv) keeps every code-dependent choice as a labelled variant with an explicit degradation